(334802, 24873, 8488, '<td valign="top">I absolutely adore this image, but it gets a 9 instead of a 10 from me because nothing in it is *quite* in focus, unfortunately.</td>', 'I absolutely adore this image, but it gets a 9 instead of a 10 from me because nothing in it is *quite* in focus, unfortunately.', '2003-06-22 13:36:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(334831, 24559, 1880, '<td valign="top">This is a well done photograph. It meets the challenge as the subject  is a tad off center which greatly enhances the composition. The colors are vivid, the focus and DOF are very good for a macro. The background is very black without noticible flaws. This  is difficult to attain but is a must due to the deep DOF necessary to make this photograph work. Conratulations on a job wonderful image. - 10 - RLS</td>', 'This is a well done photograph. It meets the challenge as the subject  is a tad off center which greatly enhances the composition. The colors are vivid, the focus and DOF are very good for a macro. The background is very black without noticible flaws. This  is difficult to attain but is a must due to the deep DOF necessary to make this photograph work. Conratulations on a job wonderful image. - 10 - RLS', '2003-06-22 14:05:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(334833, 24728, 1880, '<td valign="top">This is my favorite image of the challenge. The selection of props and location is impeccable. Your command over the use of light makes this photograph outstanding. The shadows seem perfect and the highlights outstanding.Without proper placement and use of light the delicate detail within the shadows and highlights could easily be lost. You have managed to not only preserve this detail but to use it to your advantage through the placement of the props.  The combinations of hues and objects fit like a hand in a glove.  Not many photographers understand how to assemble proper props to create a still life with impact but you have displayed great command of that skill with this image. Congratulations on your submission - 10 - RLS</td>', 'This is my favorite image of the challenge. The selection of props and location is impeccable. Your command over the use of light makes this photograph outstanding. The shadows seem perfect and the highlights outstanding.Without proper placement and use of light the delicate detail within the shadows and highlights could easily be lost. You have managed to not only preserve this detail but to use it to your advantage through the placement of the props.  The combinations of hues and objects fit like a hand in a glove.  Not many photographers understand how to assemble proper props to create a still life with impact but you have displayed great command of that skill with this image. Congratulations on your submission - 10 - RLS', '2003-06-22 14:07:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(334836, 24901, 1880, '<td valign="top">The placement of the subject in this photograph meets the challenge as the musician is off center. The total blur effect, which I believe to be purposely used, in this photograph confuses me when I look at this photograph. I would like to suggest next time you attempt to capture most of the image in focus while using the hands strumming the instrument to show the movement blur. This would have had a better impact for me. I must give you a 4 for this effort. RLS</td>', 'The placement of the subject in this photograph meets the challenge as the musician is off center. The total blur effect, which I believe to be purposely used, in this photograph confuses me when I look at this photograph. I would like to suggest next time you attempt to capture most of the image in focus while using the hands strumming the instrument to show the movement blur. This would have had a better impact for me. I must give you a 4 for this effort. RLS', '2003-06-22 14:15:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(334840, 24745, 1880, '<td valign="top">This image meets the challenge as the chair is off center. I do find what I consider to be flaws with this image thoough.  There appears to be a large amount of lens flare around the door handles. Use of a lens hood may have negated that effect. If the chair is meant to be the subject of the composition it needs to be brought into better focus. The reflection from the front leg of the chair is also distracting. I believe better control of your lighting would have helped this photograph.  The elements you have attempted to combine as a composition and the choice of lighting situations make creating a photograph with impact difficult to accomplish to say the least.  I must give you a 4 for thi challenge. RLS</td>', 'This image meets the challenge as the chair is off center. I do find what I consider to be flaws with this image thoough.  There appears to be a large amount of lens flare around the door handles. Use of a lens hood may have negated that effect. If the chair is meant to be the subject of the composition it needs to be brought into better focus. The reflection from the front leg of the chair is also distracting. I believe better control of your lighting would have helped this photograph.  The elements you have attempted to combine as a composition and the choice of lighting situations make creating a photograph with impact difficult to accomplish to say the least.  I must give you a 4 for thi challenge. RLS', '2003-06-22 14:23:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(334856, 24523, 8911, '<td valign="top">I like this, particularly the fact that the tree trunk and shadow in the upper right corner has been used to "balance" the photo, without pulling attention from the actual subject. I do wish I could tell what the critter partway down the right side is. :)</td>', 'I like this, particularly the fact that the tree trunk and shadow in the upper right corner has been used to "balance" the photo, without pulling attention from the actual subject. I do wish I could tell what the critter partway down the right side is. :)', '2003-06-22 15:10:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(334899, 24984, 2923, '<td valign="top">Not sure if this works well as a off center subject, the reflection makes me want to view the entire boat.</td>', 'Not sure if this works well as a off center subject, the reflection makes me want to view the entire boat.', '2003-06-22 17:12:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(334904, 24735, 8911, '<td valign="top">That must have taken a bit of timing or work to get. The bit of someone''s head (I think it is) near the bottom is distracting. (It also seems to give lie to the angle chosen for the photograph, making it a bit less dramatic to my eyes, at least.)</td>', 'That must have taken a bit of timing or work to get. The bit of someone''s head (I think it is) near the bottom is distracting. (It also seems to give lie to the angle chosen for the photograph, making it a bit less dramatic to my eyes, at least.)', '2003-06-22 17:51:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(334909, 24637, 8911, '<td valign="top">Nice concept. I''m kind of sorry to see the fan blend into the background, though - if it had been much darker, or otherwise stood out against the sky, it might have made a more imposing subject. The blurring of the fan blades - neither so much as to render them unrecognizable, nor so little as to suggest it''s off - is nice.</td>', 'Nice concept. I''m kind of sorry to see the fan blend into the background, though - if it had been much darker, or otherwise stood out against the sky, it might have made a more imposing subject. The blurring of the fan blades - neither so much as to render them unrecognizable, nor so little as to suggest it''s off - is nice.', '2003-06-22 18:16:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(334920, 24948, 5044, '<td valign="top">i like it but wish the perspective was from just a bit lower. That way you would have seen the entire leafy part of the tree against the blue sky.</td>', 'i like it but wish the perspective was from just a bit lower. That way you would have seen the entire leafy part of the tree against the blue sky.', '2003-06-22 18:46:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(334922, 24758, 5044, '<td valign="top">too bad about that little speck on the left. Touch it up for a print. NIce shot. perhaps a little too much USM as you can really see the "jaggies" on your edges.</td>', 'too bad about that little speck on the left. Touch it up for a print. NIce shot. perhaps a little too much USM as you can really see the "jaggies" on your edges.', '2003-06-22 18:49:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(334952, 24780, 8911, '<td valign="top">If it weren''t for the bit of white, I''d swear this was a picture of my parents'' cat. Terribly cute - a nice catch on that tongue! I''m also impressed that the cat is cmpletely clear against the background, and still not miscolored from it. The light caught the left eye a bit, so the pupil is yellowed, but I didn''t catch that till staring closely.</td>', 'If it weren''t for the bit of white, I''d swear this was a picture of my parents'' cat. Terribly cute - a nice catch on that tongue! I''m also impressed that the cat is cmpletely clear against the background, and still not miscolored from it. The light caught the left eye a bit, so the pupil is yellowed, but I didn''t catch that till staring closely.', '2003-06-22 19:33:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(334969, 24412, 8637, '<td valign="top">Off center but out of focus..</td>', 'Off center but out of focus..', '2003-06-22 19:56:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(334971, 24923, 8637, '<td valign="top">Very nice shot although little more DOF would help...perhaps focus more to the center of the object if possible.  thanks</td>', 'Very nice shot although little more DOF would help...perhaps focus more to the center of the object if possible.  thanks', '2003-06-22 19:57:58.000000', NULL, 1),
