(335825, 24395, 6202, '<td valign="top">Critique Club<br/> <br/>I really do like this image it is a very nice off centered entry.  The blue and white contrast each other nicely.  <br/> <br/>The one thing that does hurt the overall look is the "halo" effect that you got, which appears to be mostly along the rope and only slightly on the ring itself, as I look at it I can''t decide if that was from an unsharpening mask or if that was the motion of it being tossed.<br/> <br/>Anyhow it really is a cool image and nice composition, definately fit the challenge.<br/> <br/>Anna</td>', 'Critique Club I really do like this image it is a very nice off centered entry.  The blue and white contrast each other nicely.   The one thing that does hurt the overall look is the "halo" effect that you got, which appears to be mostly along the rope and only slightly on the ring itself, as I look at it I can''t decide if that was from an unsharpening mask or if that was the motion of it being tossed. Anyhow it really is a cool image and nice composition, definately fit the challenge. Anna', '2003-06-23 19:19:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(335851, 24395, 1863, '<td valign="top">Let me make things a bit clear :) For OneSweetSin and anybody else who was curious. This photo was taken at about 6 am in the pool outside my flat. It was placed in still water, and I took a few pictures. The "halo" effect is the water, I guess. YOu can see a line on the life saver which IS the water, if that''s what you mean by halo... ?<br/> <br/>Thanks for the comments everybody, <br/>Annida</td>', 'Let me make things a bit clear :) For OneSweetSin and anybody else who was curious. This photo was taken at about 6 am in the pool outside my flat. It was placed in still water, and I took a few pictures. The "halo" effect is the water, I guess. YOu can see a line on the life saver which IS the water, if that''s what you mean by halo... ? Thanks for the comments everybody, Annida', '2003-06-23 19:38:52.000000', NULL, 0),
