(336055, 24395, 4494, '<td valign="top">Annida,<br/> <br/>The halo is the line around the subject, that kind of seperates it from the background...  You can see it as a light color next to the blue parts of the life-preserver, and a darker color near the light colors (of the preserver).  Your pic may have been "challenged" because of this (because it could be sign that the subject was cut and pasted onto a background), but can also be due to a lot of other things, like over-use of Unsharp Mask in particular, etc.<br/> <br/>I really like the simplicity of the shot.  I noticed the "halo" myself, but figured it was due to something other then cheating.<br/></td>', 'Annida, The halo is the line around the subject, that kind of seperates it from the background...  You can see it as a light color next to the blue parts of the life-preserver, and a darker color near the light colors (of the preserver).  Your pic may have been "challenged" because of this (because it could be sign that the subject was cut and pasted onto a background), but can also be due to a lot of other things, like over-use of Unsharp Mask in particular, etc. I really like the simplicity of the shot.  I noticed the "halo" myself, but figured it was due to something other then cheating.', '2003-06-24 02:05:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(336061, 24395, 1863, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ChrisW123:</b></div><hr/><i>Annida,<br/> <br/>The halo is the line around the subject, that kind of seperates it from the background...  You can see it as a light color next to the blue parts of the life-preserver, and a darker color near the light colors (of the preserver).  Your pic may have been "challenged" because of this (because it could be sign that the subject was cut and pasted onto a background), but can also be due to a lot of other things, like over-use of Unsharp Mask in particular, etc.<br/> <br/>I really like the simplicity of the shot.  I noticed the "halo" myself, but figured it was due to something other then cheating.</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I think I''m going crazy, cause I just can''t see the halo. I"m going all googly eyed staring at this picture! lol</td>', 'Originally posted by ChrisW123:Annida, The halo is the line around the subject, that kind of seperates it from the background...  You can see it as a light color next to the blue parts of the life-preserver, and a darker color near the light colors (of the preserver).  Your pic may have been "challenged" because of this (because it could be sign that the subject was cut and pasted onto a background), but can also be due to a lot of other things, like over-use of Unsharp Mask in particular, etc. I really like the simplicity of the shot.  I noticed the "halo" myself, but figured it was due to something other then cheating.  I think I''m going crazy, cause I just can''t see the halo. I"m going all googly eyed staring at this picture! lol', '2003-06-24 02:37:19.000000', NULL, 0),
