(336412, 24559, 2667, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the win JJ! I looked for some info on that critter, but couldn''t find anything specific. I''m sure he is some kind of hornworm, but I don''t know if we have any that look like that around here. So I have no idea what kind of moth or butterfly he is in training for!</td>', 'Congrats on the win JJ! I looked for some info on that critter, but couldn''t find anything specific. I''m sure he is some kind of hornworm, but I don''t know if we have any that look like that around here. So I have no idea what kind of moth or butterfly he is in training for!', '2003-06-24 14:32:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(336421, 24985, 3790, '<td valign="top">Great shot. Are you going to make this one available in DPCPrints? I have some racing enthusiast friends who would love it.</td>', 'Great shot. Are you going to make this one available in DPCPrints? I have some racing enthusiast friends who would love it.', '2003-06-24 14:46:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(336427, 24926, 7033, '<td valign="top">Thanks to everyone for the comments... <br/> <br/>I originally shot the entire tractor/baler/platform off-center, but it didn''t really give the entire scene the perspective I was hoping to achieve.  By cropping down to include just the part of the scene in my challenge submission, it brought the focus back to the tractor and enhanced the composition, in my opinion.<br/> <br/>As for the comments about the sharpness, I''m not certain exactly what to think.  On my calibrated monitors at home and work, it looks fine, but I did notice that at my Dad''s house, it brought out more of the effect of sharpening.  He runs a much lower color setting and resolution, though, so perhaps that''s the difference.</td>', 'Thanks to everyone for the comments...  I originally shot the entire tractor/baler/platform off-center, but it didn''t really give the entire scene the perspective I was hoping to achieve.  By cropping down to include just the part of the scene in my challenge submission, it brought the focus back to the tractor and enhanced the composition, in my opinion. As for the comments about the sharpness, I''m not certain exactly what to think.  On my calibrated monitors at home and work, it looks fine, but I did notice that at my Dad''s house, it brought out more of the effect of sharpening.  He runs a much lower color setting and resolution, though, so perhaps that''s the difference.', '2003-06-24 14:56:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(336437, 24901, 1897, '<td valign="top">I think the thing that bothers me, is the position of the mike stand.  It really intrudes on the flowing colors of this image,</td>', 'I think the thing that bothers me, is the position of the mike stand.  It really intrudes on the flowing colors of this image,', '2003-06-24 15:16:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(336513, 24985, 5904, '<td valign="top">Thank you all for the comments.  This was one of those goofy "no thought" shots that just seemed to pop.  Yes, I plan to put it up on DCPrints as soon as I have a spare moment to do it right.<br/> <br/>Ru</td>', 'Thank you all for the comments.  This was one of those goofy "no thought" shots that just seemed to pop.  Yes, I plan to put it up on DCPrints as soon as I have a spare moment to do it right. Ru', '2003-06-24 16:55:26.000000', NULL, 0),
